WEBVTT

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.220
Please excuse me.

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:17.580
Mahiro-san, you had better wake 
up soon or you'll be late.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.820
Karin, Karen.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:22.840
Understood.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:23.990
Sure thing!

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.760
Just look at this place. It's a complete mess.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.170
Good morning, Yayoi-chan.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:38.010
Oh, are you staying in the loft?

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.760
But your bed is over here.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:46.240
Gosh, clean that up at once.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:50.480
No, it's okay. It's fun because 
it's like a big toy box.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.580
Keeping one's room tidy and organized 
is one of the dorm rules.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.230
You mustn't baby her.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:59.680
Mistress, I think you do quite 
a lot of babying yourself.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.010
It's only for today!

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:04.000
And that's only because she 
absolutely cannot be late today.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:09.120
Even if I am a night owl, 
an all-night cram session is still tough.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.000
Cram session?

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:16.010
Today we have midterms.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.090
What are those?

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.330
Th-They're tests?!

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.490
First period: Japanese

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.490
Second period: Science

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.490
Third period: Sociology

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.490
Fourth period: Mathematics

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.050
Hey, are you still alive?

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.040
You're better off not worrying about it.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.850
You'll be fine as long as you don't fail.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.450
W-What's a fail?

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.500
Below 40%.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.640
I don't think that helped.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.740
I should have told her about the tests.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.500
It was out of your hands, Mistress.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.010
After all, Lion was out like a 
light yesterday after that bath.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:28.830
In any event, she couldn't have done 
anything with only one night.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:31.280
She could have had an 
all-night cram session.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.920
You'd be better off not 
getting into that habit.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:36.520
You have to study a little bit every day!

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:37.420
Growl

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.290
Lion, what are you doing for lunch?

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.650
I'm going to buy some food!

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.770
<i>I hardly knew any of it at all.</i>

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.800
<i>I did try to put some 
kind of answer down though.</i>

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:02.790
Goodness gracious.

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:05.770
Yuko-senpai.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.200
What's the matter, Lion-chan?

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.920
You don't look at all happy.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:14.910
You can tell?

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:15.890
Of course.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:18.440
If something's the matter, 
I'm happy to listen.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:21.940
Senpai!

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.010
Goodness gracious.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:30.700
Oh?

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.460
So you're worried about 
your scores on your tests?

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:36.420
First years are so innocent.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:38.550
In any event, Lion-kun,

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:43.540
Yuko's pillowy parts 
all belong to me.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:44.700
Mizuki.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.760
But...

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:51.210
Lion-chan, you don't have to listen 
to anything she has to say.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.770
Say aah!

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:58.760
Delicious!

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.860
A smile suits you best.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.880
Oink for me!

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.260
Oink!

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.820
Very good. I like girls who are obedient.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.190
Come now, Mizuki.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.430
Hmph.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.690
Even if you're joking, 
you're the student council president,

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:20.100
so you shouldn't be teasing a first year.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.260
You're the student council president?

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.440
That's right.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.270
Amongst all the students, 
I'm the most important.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:27.630
Revere me.

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:30.570
Mizuki.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:37.800
So I'm the student council president.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.610
Yuko is the vice president.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.420
Aoi over there is the treasurer.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.160
Next to her is Ashley, the secretary.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:44.900
Pleased to meet you.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.310
They're both transfers.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:49.040
Transfers?

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:50.760
You've never heard of them?

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.330
They're Logicalists on 
active duty who transferred

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.500
into our school because 
it's so peaceful now.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:01.340
Personally, I think of being here as 
an opportunity to retrain myself.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:05.880
There are lots of books here and 
documents from other worlds.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.140
It makes me very happy.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.150
In other words, peace has given 
us a lot to be grateful for.

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:13.910
It lets us all relax over tea 
like what we're doing right now.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:17.610
What's the matter?

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.450
Nina-chan…

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:22.610
Right. Nina-chan's a transfer too.

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:28.370
I was thinking it'd be nice if 
Nina-chan also enjoyed being here.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.550
I think so too.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.280
<b>Empty</b>

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.780
Today, we'll be having a mock battle.

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:39.370
Lion-san, you'll start by watching.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:40.200
Okay!

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:49.020
All right, let's do this! Qipao!

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:53.150
<i>What will I do with you? Now do your best.</i>

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:11.280
How do you like my Trance with Qipao?

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.860
<i>It's so cool!</i>

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:15.030
But of course it is!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:18.330
Lend me your strength, Amor.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:21.270
<i>Sure. As long as I can be with you.</i>

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:27.390
Mock battle, start!

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:35.560
Look out!

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:39.590
Huh?

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:40.830
It's okay.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:43.770
There's no way any of you 
could get hurt doing this.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:54.160
Whoever removes their opponent's 
six defensive shields first wins.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:58.340
Do you know why we carry 
out these mock battles?

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:00.170
To get stronger?

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:02.440
To understand your own powers better.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.170
With the powers you all possess,

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.910
if you put your mind to it, 
you could easily hurt others

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:09.340
or destroy anything you wanted to.

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:12.290
Despite that, in the majority of countries,

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:15.180
Logicalists and Foreigners have 
the right to move about freely,

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.150
with no restrictions on the use of their trance.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.340
Why do you think that's the case?

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:23.420
Because they're all good people?

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:24.930
Close.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:28.940
The answer is because Logicalists 
fought against the bad Foreigners,

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.950
and preserved peace for everyone.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:36.630
Many of your senpais and good Foreigners 
have built a relationship of trust.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:40.240
Lion-san, I hope that you will
help to protect that trust.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.110
I will!

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:52.170
Miss Ricchan, you're not going to Trance?

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.390
I've no reason to today, do I?

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:57.060
Aw, I wanted to see it.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:58.090
Come on.

00:08:58.090 --> 00:09:00.770
Try not to push your elders around too much.

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.510
Miss Kagura!

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:07.500
Logicalists' powers gradually 
fade away once you hit 20.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:12.530
The statistics suggest that it becomes quite 
difficult to Trance once you hit around 30.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:13.700
So Ricchan…

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:15.080
Roar

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.570
Still 24

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:21.940
Mahiro-san?

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:26.310
I can still quite easily Trance.

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:28.460
Calm down, Fujisaki.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.460
Lion, let's go. We're ready now.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:34.550
Let's start your contract.

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.990
<i>Lion, can you hear me?</i>

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:45.810
Yes.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.180
<i>Take out your card.</i>

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:55.110
Foreigner Cards connect our world, 
Septpia, to other worlds.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.300
They can open a gate and call 
Foreigners to our world.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:01.650
<i>We're going to register the Foreigner 
you're contracted to to that card now.</i>

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:04.320
<i>Her name is Rosa.</i>

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:06.330
Rosa.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:09.020
You're a pretty special case.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.060
Apparently you made a contract with 
her when you were around 2 years old.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:15.430
<i>This is ALCA's database.</i>

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:18.970
<i>Here we research Foreigner's 
abilities and dispositions.</i>

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.060
<i>One can also apply for a contract here.</i>

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:24.320
<i>Those who already have a contract 
can't apply for another,</i>

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:27.140
<i>and if one's Logic doesn't fit the 
contract, it will be refused.</i>

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:34.230
<i>Normally, finding a contractor is the 
biggest barrier for a Logicalist.</i>

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:36.920
So Rosa's not registered, huh?

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:41.100
<i>Lion, look at your card and try calling her.</i>

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:42.960
Rosa.

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:50.420
Be more forceful. Call out from your heart.

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:53.340
Your contractor will absolutely 
answer your call.

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:56.570
Rosa.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:58.850
Rosa.

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:17.590
So the woman back then was you?

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:21.050
Your cries echo far.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.230
They echo here, as well.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:28.060
Please, lend me your strength.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:32.560
Please! I want to stay with Nina-chan.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.400
With my friends.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.940
Did you make friends?

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:39.130
Yeah.

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:40.510
I see.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:42.890
Don't hurt yourself now.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:53.020
Gate Access! Monolium!

00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:57.170
I'm counting on you, Rosa.

00:11:57.170 --> 00:12:00.140
<i>Lion, as long as you wish it.</i>

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:32.090
<i>Miss Kagura! I formed the contract!</i>

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.440
You did, huh?

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:38.570
Well, I suppose you'll need to 
practice for a while.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:39.310
<i>Of course!</i>

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:44.320
Episode 2

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:44.320
Transforming is Not Mastered in a Day

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:47.320
Episode 2

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:47.320
Rice Balls Over Flowers

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:51.570
Now then, I'm going to hand out your 
results for the mathematics midterm.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.330
First Year Mathematics Midterm Test

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.330
Class S      Liones Yelistratova

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.330
<b>15% 
Let's try harder
 next time.</b>

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:04.760
The average was 70%. I suppose that's okay.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:08.260
The students who got 
perfect scores were Yayoi and…

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:09.820
Nina.

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:12.270
You did a good job studying.

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:26.300
Nina Alexandrovna.

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:32.220
As of today, you will be assigned to 
the Logicalist school Pirari Academy.

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:37.090
Taking your age into account, your actual 
enrollment will begin this spring.

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:41.170
Of course, you need not take the entrance 
exam, and will transfer into the S class.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:47.520
Bureau Chief Veronica, I've finished 
studying all the fundamental subjects.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:48.920
Indeed.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:52.170
I understand that you have the academic 
capabilities of a university graduate

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:56.030
and are a Logicalist 
with several contractors.

00:13:56.030 --> 00:14:01.360
Then why? Why do I have to go to 
a Logicalist training academy?

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:04.730
Because there's something
 you need to learn.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:07.270
What… could that be?

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:11.000
You're still young. I want 
you to understand that.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.500
I'd appreciate a more logical answer.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:16.790
Are you trying to tell me that I'm weak?

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:19.380
In a way, yes.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.090
Understood.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.400
However, I am not convinced.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:29.000
When I have proven my strength,

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.460
I will apply to be reinstated 
to my previous mission.

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:39.860
Nina-chan?

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:41.220
Nina-chan?

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:43.010
What's the matter?

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:46.610
It's nothing.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.980
Hey Nina-chan, let's go 
cherry blossom viewing.

00:14:50.270 --> 00:14:53.870
Cherry blossoms? Haven't the 
petals all fallen by now?

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.700
There's still some late-blooming 
cherry blossom trees left.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:00.750
Apparently Mahiro-chan grew up around 
here, so she knows all about it.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:03.910
Oh, are you going to the 
shrine up in the mountains?

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:09.220
Yeah. Lion said she'd never seen 
cherry blossoms before, so I'm taking her.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.220
How about you, Yacchan?

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.440
We're going this Saturday.

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:16.890
I have business to attend to 
at the Tachibana household.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:19.570
Yayoi-chan, you're going back home?

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:24.560
Yes. My house is close to the academy, 
so I can be there and back in a day.

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:26.350
Allow me to explain.

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.990
The Tachibana family is a renowned family

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.200
with a storied history that 
goes back over a thousand years.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.200
But they aren't aristocrats or anything.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:37.540
<b>Merchant</b>

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.530
They were amazing merchants, and 
they have lots and lots of money!

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:38.570
That's right.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:44.380
Tachibana Corporation

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:44.390
Presently, the Tachibana family is a worldwide 
financial conglomerate with 100 branch offices.

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:47.670
Our HQ is right here, in Obihiro.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.670
HQ

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:50.610
In order to cooperate with the 
founding of Pirari Academy,

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:54.670
my great, great grandfather moved here.

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:56.300
Wow.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:57.690
Our family motto is,

00:15:57.690 --> 00:16:01.380
"Any profits from trade should 
be used on people everywhere."

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:06.100
"The more rich the world gets, the 
more profit there is to gain."

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:10.450
The Kiritani family has 
protected the Tachibanas for generations.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:12.450
So of course we accompany her everywhere.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:15.710
We're the ones who protect our mistress!

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:18.490
Yayoi-chan, you're amazing.

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:21.680
I don't know how to take that,
coming from a princess.

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:25.040
Rin-chan, Ren-chan, will you come 
see cherry blossoms with us?

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:29.450
I'm very sorry to say we will be 
staying at our mistress's side,

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:32.220
so you three will have to enjoy 
the flowers without us.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:33.070
Okay.

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:37.530
Mahiro-chan, Nina-chan, 
let's go together.

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:38.820
Got it!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:40.630
Huh?

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:52.980
But I never said I'd go.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.670
<i>I have to prove my strength.</i>

00:16:58.290 --> 00:16:59.470
<i>But how?</i>

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.950
Goodness, it's Nina-chan.

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:07.470
Good evening. Do you mind if I join you?

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:09.960
Please.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:30.480
You're going with Lion-chan to see 
the cherry blossoms, aren't you?

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:32.340
I'm…

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:34.730
Why not? It should be fun for a change.

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:38.400
I'll be sure to make you a delicious lunch.

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:58.770
Yuko-senpai, thank you very much!

00:17:58.770 --> 00:17:59.870
It was nothing.

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:02.480
I'm happy that the weather looks so good.

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:03.400
Yeah!

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:05.680
Have a safe trip.

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:06.980
Okay!

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:08.430
We'll be back.

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:10.950
Nina-chan, have fun.

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:12.860
I'll be back.

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.810
So there's a shrine all the way up here?

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:22.540
It's a small little place 
that nobody usually goes to.

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:26.310
The patron god of the area is enshrined 
elsewhere, towards Pirari Town.

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:29.300
Look at this reaction.

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:31.370
There's got to be something close by!

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:39.330
Come on, it's not like my 
stuff blows up all the time!

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:42.420
Belle says it's dangerous, too.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:46.180
<i>But she hasn't had anything 
blow up yet today.</i>

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.500
Here it comes! Here it comes!

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.190
The Paradox Level is...

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:52.760
pretty high!

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:55.690
What? What kind is it? 
Is it an amazing Foreigner?

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:00.300
I knew it.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.920
You can eat these.

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:30.960
She's good.

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:32.130
She is.

00:19:35.930 --> 00:19:37.530
<i>So fluffy.</i>

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.240
So pretty.

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.120
Now this is a cherry blossom viewing!

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:55.720
First off…

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:57.710
It's gotta be rice balls over flowers!

00:19:57.710 --> 00:19:59.040
What is that?

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:02.530
It's a pain to eat it bit by bit, so I 
asked Yuko-senpai to put it all in one!

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:08.930
She's really an amazing cook!

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:10.810
Want to try a bite?

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:13.230
No. I've got my own.

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:15.480
<b>For 
Nina-chan</b>

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:19.090
<i>So cute.</i>

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:28.340
<i>I-I can't move.</i>

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:34.170
<i>Today I was supposed to do some 
training and study battle tactics.</i>

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:41.910
<i>She's kind of like a dog.</i>

00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:47.800
<i>Every so often, as long as it's 
not too often, this kind of thing</i>

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:48.990
<i>might be good for a change.</i>

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:22.780
Sake

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:27.640
I've got nothing but interesting 
students this year.

00:23:00.530 --> 00:23:03.630
She always spends her time off 
just sleeping or drinking.

00:23:03.630 --> 00:23:06.330
But today of all days, 
she tells me she's busy?

00:23:06.590 --> 00:23:09.940
It gets pretty lonely when your usual 
partner is missing, doesn't it?

00:23:09.940 --> 00:23:11.440
It does!

00:23:11.440 --> 00:23:14.590
And here I went out of my way to 
set aside the alcohol she likes.

00:23:14.590 --> 00:23:16.740
So what's she busy with?

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:18.740
She's on a date.

00:23:18.740 --> 00:23:20.700
I'm just going to drink it all!

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:29.780
Next Episode

00:23:20.700 --> 00:23:22.910
Wh-Wh-What kind of person is he?

00:23:22.910 --> 00:23:24.880
Sharp-eyed and sexy?

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:26.800
But he's sweet when it comes to her,

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:29.170
and it's like they get along so 
well there's no room for me.

00:23:29.190 --> 00:23:30.680
How tall is he? How much does he make?

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:32.510
He's taller than her.

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:35.300
I really don't know how much he makes, 
but he seems like he might be rich.

00:23:35.300 --> 00:23:39.760
I'd really like to meet him! 
If possible, a mixer would be great!
